    "description": "Vintage Electrical Insulator Lot - 14 Pieces\nHemingray, Brookfield, H.G. Co., Locke\nAqua, Green, Clear Glass and Brown Ceramic, Late 19th to Mid-20th Century\nComprehensive collection of 14 vintage telegraph and electrical power line insulators, featuring classic pressed glass and glazed ceramic examples from prominent American manufacturers including Hemingray, Brookfield, and Locke. These heavy industrial relics showcase the technological evolution of American infrastructure, valued for their sculptural ribbed forms, embossed lettering, and rich glass colorations.\nPieces Included:\nHemingray-42 glass insulator, aqua teal with drip points\nHemingray-42 glass insulator, clear with drip points\nHemingray-19 glass insulator, aqua teal with drip points\nHemingray-56 glass insulator, clear ribbed design\nHemingray-17 glass insulator, clear compact design\nBrookfield glass insulator, deep green teal\nH.G. CO. glass pony insulator, dark teal green\nLocke porcelain saddle-top insulator, dark brown glaze\nBrown glazed ceramic high-voltage pin insulator\n5 additional Hemingray and related style glass insulators in aqua and green\nCondition:\nAuthentic vintage field-used condition. The glass and porcelain retain glossy surfaces with varied fleabiting, small wire-wear chips, and surface abrasions typical of retired utility line hardware. Embossing remains clear and legible across marked pieces.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
